WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.450
Speaker 1: Speaking of violence, we haven't
done this for a while and and I think it's

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.769
important to do it again.

00:00:06.769 --> 00:00:11.080
Did you know that there were 10 mass shootings
this past weekend, just this past weekend

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.309
that finished a couple of days ago?

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:17.070
The Gun Violence Archive tracks mass shootings.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:23.930
And on June 4th, 5th and 6th, there were 10
individual shooting incidents in which a minimum

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:31.460
of four victims were shot, either injured
or killed, not including any shooter who may

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.870
have also been injured or killed during the
incident.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:41.140
This is 10 incidents where at least four people
were killed and or injured.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.340
And consider for a second by this definition
of mass shooting where you need at least four

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.930
injuries or deaths.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:53.270
There were a whole bunch of other incidents
with two or three people being injured and

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:59.290
killed when the baseline is set at four injured
and killed.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:04.260
We had 10 such incidents this past weekend
and it barely made news.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.460
It is just another normal weekend in the United
States of America.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.460
Some examples.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:14.829
In Portland, Oregon, four were killed and
one were injured at a home in Indianapolis,

00:01:14.829 --> 00:01:15.829
Indiana.

00:01:15.829 --> 00:01:22.240
Two were killed and two were injured, all
in the parking lot of a Boston market restaurant

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.780
in North Carolina.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.450
Four people were shot and injured at a party
at a trailer park.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:32.420
And I could go through and give you all of
the various stories.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.189
But you can imagine how all of these or many
of these went down.

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:44.020
But 10 mass shootings this weekend and it
barely makes news because it has become background

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.020
noise.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:49.780
That's the tragic reality of the situation,
the loss of life, the injury.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.049
That's one tragedy.

00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:54.920
The other tragedy is that this stuff barely
even makes the news anymore.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.969
Another weekend, another 10 mass shootings,
and the number is probably more like 25 if

00:01:58.969 --> 00:02:02.880
you include those where two or three people
were injured as well.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.299
Also, it's embarrassing.

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:06.409
It's not just tragic.

00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:07.409
It's embarrassing.

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:09.829
The world looks at us clearly.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.079
We have the resources for dealing with this.

00:02:12.079 --> 00:02:13.819
It's not a money issue.

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:17.840
We have no shortage of ideas for how to deal
with it, even, you know, without touching

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.579
the Second Amendment, which we have a Second
Amendment, OK, without even going close to

00:02:22.579 --> 00:02:27.209
infringing on the Second Amendment, we have
so many ideas for things that should be done.

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:32.670
Look at what happened on vaccines once we
got competent leadership in power in January.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.390
We clearly can do things.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.610
We clearly can manage big projects.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:39.380
There's no it's not an impossibility.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:44.510
And yet there is simply no political will
to deal with this.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.769
And it's a global embarrassment, truly.

00:02:46.769 --> 00:02:51.490
And, you know, even if you don't care about
gun violence per say, like maybe you don't,

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:56.340
do you realize how this makes us look to our
adversaries and the ideas that this gives

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.340
our adversaries?

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.870
They see another weekend, another ten mass
shootings.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:06.670
What the hell is wrong with these Americans
if the they are saying if the U.S. population

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:14.060
has been propagandized enough that they won't
do anything on guns if they can't even pass

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:19.620
one hundred percent universal background checks
when when Democrats control the House, Senate,

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.170
White House and right after the Sandy Hook
shooting.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:26.780
If they can't do that, clearly these are very
manipulatable people.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:31.549
This is one of those situations where the
world sees the insanity of this.

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:35.249
Is this not yet affecting the right people?

00:03:35.249 --> 00:03:37.239
And that's why nothing is being done.

00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:38.340
Is the.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.360
Combination of the gun profit lobby, because
that's what they are and the gun nuts, is

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.390
that combination too powerful to allow anything
to be done?

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:53.870
My issue isn't even with the firearms necessarily,
but it's with American gun culture, lack of

00:03:53.870 --> 00:04:01.060
screening, lack of enforcement of laws, lack
of of ongoing training, insurance policies

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:06.629
if you own guns, lack of access to mental
health treatment, the political movement that

00:04:06.629 --> 00:04:07.849
fetishizes guns.

00:04:07.849 --> 00:04:09.139
Yeah, OK, the guns are a problem.

00:04:09.139 --> 00:04:14.439
But what I mean is it doesn't have to be a
problem of guns necessarily.

00:04:14.439 --> 00:04:15.900
And I'm being careful with the wording here.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:21.930
In our case, it is a problem of guns, but
also of all of those other things that I mentioned.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.100
And the world sees it.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.870
And it's humiliating.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.000
It's tragic.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.050
It's embarrassing.

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:29.890
And there is no I mean, I wish I had any optimism.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.830
I have no optimism, you know, OK, Biden announced
some stuff.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:38.430
They're going to be he is directing the creation
of certain groups to look at, OK, it was an

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:42.730
effort, but most of that is just, hey, please
look into this type stuff.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:45.700
I am not optimistic on this issue at all.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.460
If you are, let me know why.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:49.460
Let me know why.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:50.530
I should be more optimistic.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:05:02.430
You can find me on Twitter 

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:07.380
at David Pakman

